              "This view is shared by pro-trade lobbyists in the U.S., who have accused Trump of misunderstanding tariff payments. Trump has repeatedly said that Chinese exporters will bear the brunt, but a common refrain in recent weeks among trade lobbyists is that “tariffs are a tax on U.S. consumers”.\n\n“Forcing American consumers to pay more for clothes, shoes, toys, electronics and even food will do nothing to hold China accountable,” read a statement from Tariffs Hurt the Heartland, a lobby group",
